			"widgets_values":[
				"subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is Zhu Di, a 16-year-old Ming prince with sharp eyes and a proud bearing, whose appearance comes from <Picture 1>, wearing a dark-green brocade robe and holding a wooden bow.\n<Subject 2> is Crown Prince Zhu Biao, a 24-year-old gentle and dignified prince, whose appearance comes from <Picture 2>, wearing a pale-yellow prince robe.\n<Subject 3> is the Hongwu Emperor Zhu Yuanzhang, stern and majestic, whose appearance comes from <Picture 3>.\n<Subject 4> is the imperial garden in spring, whose layout comes from <Picture 4>, with palace walls, stone railings, a distant tree trunk, and dappled shade.\n<Picture 5> is the second scene, a palace hall interior.\n<Picture 6> is the opening prologue, the imperial city under dark clouds.\n<Picture 7> is the third scene, a side chamber.\n<Picture 8> is the fourth scene, a night hall with candles.\n<Picture 9> is the finale, a night silhouette.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] One continuous shot in the imperial garden: <Subject 1> stands in dappled shade holding a bow, scolds kneeling eunuchs with a measured line, releases an arrow that strikes a distant tree trunk, then <Subject 2> steps out of the sunlight and speaks to him.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - the young prince's face, dark-green brocade robe, and wooden bow remain identical to <Picture 1>.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - the crown prince's face and pale-yellow robe remain identical to <Picture 2>.\n<Subject 4> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - the garden layout, palace wall, stone railing, and tree remain identical to <Picture 4>.\n<Picture 3>, <Picture 5>, <Picture 6>, <Picture 7>, <Picture 8>, <Picture 9>: weak_reference - these references guide only appearance and style, not the current shot.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video uses a cinematic historical live-action style with dappled spring light, a desaturated warm palette, and a steady fixed camera; no text overlays, no watermarks, no extra people.\n[Shot 1] A medium shot at eye level with a fixed camera, no pan and no drift. <Subject 1> (S1), the 16-year-old prince in the dark-green brocade robe holding the wooden bow, stands in dappled shade among the stone railings of <Subject 4>; several kneeling eunuchs with disheveled hair and clothing face him. <Subject 1> (S1) speaks in a youthful but sharp voice at a measured pace, his lips moving naturally with every word, <d>[Chinese] 议论国事，本无过错。错的是，你们身在深宫，眼界方寸，竟敢妄议边疆将士生死。</d> He closes his lips, his faint smile fades, and his eyes turn sharp. He strokes the bowstring once with his right hand, raises the bow, and releases an arrow; the arrow flies straight along the sight line and strikes a distant tree trunk, the shaft vibrating on impact. The camera remains fixed. <Subject 2> (S2), the 24-year-old crown prince in the pale-yellow robe, walks out of warm sunlight from the right toward <Subject 1>; the two-shot keeps a clear light/shadow split across their faces. <Subject 2> (S2) speaks in a gentle resigned voice, his lips moving naturally, <d>[Chinese] 老四，又在恃强欺人？</d> He closes his lips with a mild sigh. The camera pulls back slowly, then holds. Throughout the shot the camera stays stable: no drifting, no floating motion, no unnecessary zoom.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nSoft spring garden ambience continues throughout: gentle birdsong, distant palace bells, and faint wind in the leaves; the eunuchs murmur quietly in fear, the bowstring twangs, and the arrow thuds into the tree trunk.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nLow solemn Chinese court strings begin softly after the arrow strikes, restrained in volume, and fade out by the end."
